dillo-vm for Ubuntu Resolute
===========================

The source and binary package names are dillo-vm. The executable remains
/usr/bin/dillo, matching upstream and the Copr package. Conflicts: dillo
prevents co-installation with the unrelated Dillo browser using that path.
The supported native build architectures are amd64 and arm64.

Source preparation (network allowed)
------------------------------------

From the packaging checkout, with Git, Python 3, GNU tar, xz, and Cargo
available, run:

    debian/prepare-source /path/to/build-area

This snapshots HEAD without debian/, then runs cargo vendor --locked
--versioned-dirs against that snapshot. It writes:

    dillo-vm_0.1.0.orig.tar.xz
    dillo-vm_0.1.0.orig-vendor.tar.xz
    dillo-vm-0.1.0/             (both sources plus this debian/ directory)

Commit upstream changes before preparing sources. The current debian/
directory is copied into the build tree, so packaging changes may be tested
before committing. Use a fresh build area; existing build trees are refused.
Keep both original archives together with the .dsc and .debian.tar.xz.
The 3.0 (quilt) format extracts the second archive into vendor/. No vendor
files or generated archives are committed to the packaging branch.

The vendor component includes the generated Cargo source replacements in
vendor/config.toml. These cover both crates.io and all Git dependencies,
including development dependencies needed to resolve the locked workspace.
Regenerate both original archives together if HEAD or Cargo.lock changes.
Archive member order, owner, modes, and timestamps are normalized using
HEAD's commit time. Retain the resulting archives for subsequent package
revisions. The helper refuses to overwrite either archive or the build tree.

Offline package build
---------------------

On a native Resolute builder, install the Build-Depends from debian/control
(for example, apt-get build-dep .), then in the prepared build tree run:

    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

For an isolated build with an existing Resolute sbuild chroot, first run:

    dpkg-buildpackage -S -sa -us -uc
    sbuild --dist=resolute --arch=amd64 ../dillo-vm_0.1.0-1~resolute1.dsc

Use --arch=arm64 on a native arm64 builder. Source preparation is the only
networked Cargo operation. debian/rules uses a private CARGO_HOME, the
distribution's /usr/bin/cargo and /usr/bin/rustc, generated vendor config,
and --frozen (locked and offline). The upstream rustup toolchain pin does
not apply to those absolute tool paths. SMOLTCP_IFACE_MAX_ADDR_COUNT=4 is
required for the network backend's four interface addresses.
The -sa option includes both original archives in the source changes file.

Rust and Cargo >= 1.91 are required by the linked smoltcp dependency.
RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1 permits Cargo to parse the workspace's test-only artifact
dependencies, matching the Copr approach. Only the host dillo binary is
built; firmware and musl guest artifacts are not built. Generic debhelper
with explicit Cargo commands is used instead of dh-cargo, whose default
Debian crate registry does not represent this vendored application workspace.
The build checks dillo --help. VM tests need KVM and separate cross-built
test artifacts and are outside the package build.
The clean target preserves vendor/, including checksummed Cargo.toml.orig
files that debhelper would otherwise remove.

The package includes LICENSE, NOTICE, and the vendored crates' manifests
and accompanying license notices under /usr/share/doc/dillo-vm/.

Do not upload to Launchpad as part of this workflow. Infrastructure owns
publication to ppa:nmccallum/pichi after review.
